CI correction after native Windows run 35048517648.

The portable revision path test passed on Windows, but the same five installation-dependent tests still failed. Their only shared failing boundary was publication of the extracted staging directory.

Fix:
- Windows directory publication uses std::fs::rename for the required same-volume atomic move.
- File publication and receipt tombstones keep the existing MoveFileExW MOVEFILE_WRITE_THROUGH path.
- Reason: Microsoft documents WRITE_THROUGH as confirming copy/delete moves, while directory moves must stay on one volume.

